WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.120
We already know what Real numbers are.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.160
These are the numbers that can be represented on the number line.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.660
We also know that Real numbers can be broadly classified,

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.500
as Rational and Irrational numbers.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.860
Rational numbers are those that can be represented

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.660
as ratio of two integers with no common factor.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.180
Irrational numbers on the other hand

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.400
cannot be expressed as ratio of two integers,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.800
and when expressed in decimal notation

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.640
they are non-terminating, non-recurring decimals.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.060
Are there any other kinds of numbers?

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.720
Numbers that we haven't looked at yet.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.660
Before you answer that question,

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.980
let me ask you another one.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.880
Can you think of a number

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.520
which when squared results in a negative number?

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.040
Yes, a number which when multiplied with itself

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.840
gives a negative number.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.160
Try it!

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.040
You'd have probably tried a few options.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:08.740
'3 times 3' is 9 positive. 'Negative 5 times negative 5' is 25,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.940
again positive.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.700
'Negative root 3 times negative root 3' is 3, positive again.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.580
No luck, we'll come back to this. Don't worry!

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.200
So we've studied quadratic equations in middle school.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:27.220
We know that if x squared minus 9 is equal to 0.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.480
X is either equal to 3 or negative 3.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.500
Now try to find a solution to x squared plus 1 equal to 0.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:38.580
Not sure,

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.400
or do you think there's no solution to this one?

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:44.840
Don't worry if you couldn't get the answer to these two questions.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.360
Let's understand the situation now.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.840
Whenever we consider the square of a number say 'x'.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.220
The result was always positive,

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.200
whether the number 'x 'was a positive real

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.200
number or a negative one.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.980
We always got a positive result.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.420
And we had learned that a negative number did not have a square root.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.100
So if we had a number like negative 9

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.320
we said that it's square root did not exist.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.120
Do you remember that while finding the solution of a quadratic

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.800
equation using the formula, if the discriminant,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.180
'b squared' minus '4 ac' was negative.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.400
We said that there are no real roots of the quadratic equation.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.160
Based on what we had studied earlier

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.420
'x squared plus 1 equal to 0'

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.680
will not have any real roots as the value of

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.100
discriminant is negative 4.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.900
Why did we do this?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.580
What was the problem here?

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.000
It's easy. As the square root of negative 1 did not exist for us,

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:50.880
we said that there was no solution for the equation x squared plus 1 equals 0.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.460
However, in the 16th Century

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.060
it was a mathematician named Cardan

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.920
who first started thinking about solutions of quadratic equations

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.880
with negative discriminants.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.700
Soon others started to but it was Euler in the 18th century.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.160
Who gave the square root of negative 1

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.260
a symbol 'i' and called it the unit imaginary number.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.020
These were termed so as they were thought to be impossible

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.140
and just something we imagined.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:24.520
So 'i' was assumed to be a number whose square is negative 1.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.600
Now you'll be able to answer the two questions.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.340
Can you think of a number which when squared results in a negative number?

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.300
Yes, it's 'i'.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.280
If square root of negative 1 is 'i'.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.740
What is 'i' times 'i', or 'i' squared .

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.240
It is 'root negative 1' times 'root negative 1'.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.780
That gives us negative 1.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.540
There you go, we cut a negative number by squaring a number.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.400
And the next question was,

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.600
can you find a solution to 'x squared plus 1 equal to 0?'

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.920
The answer is yes!

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.260
Transposing one to the right-hand side,

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.080
we get x squared as negative 1.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.760
Taking the square root on both sides,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.040
we get the value of x, as root of negative 1

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.860
or minus root of Negative 1.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.380
That is plus minus 'i'.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.500
So what we learnt in school wasn't incorrect.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.380
This equation has no real roots.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.420
Yes, it has imaginary roots.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.620
That's the concept of imaginary numbers for you!

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.240
But wait, we understood the concept of square root of negative one.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.540
What if the number is square root of negative seven,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.860
or square root of negative nine?

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.060
That's what we will cover in the next video.

